System Overview
Justicar uses a pipeline architecture where a user message passes through a sequence of specialized model nodes, each producing structured output that the next node uses as context. A planner decides which nodes activate for each request. A face node delivers the final response.
The pipeline is not a single large model. It is a coordinated mesh of smaller specialized models, each doing one thing well, passing structured artifacts to the next stage.
The Planner
Role
The planner receives the user message and the tags produced by 3BM and decides the execution route for that request. It runs on Gemma — surface routing on the 2.2B model, complex routing decisions on the 9B model.
