Logging
Every node run was logged with:
Timestamp
Input received
Raw model output
Parsed structured output
Model name and quantization
Logs stored under ~/justicar/state/logs/ organized by node type.
This logging architecture was constitutional by design — the system maintained an auditable record of every decision made, every artifact produced, and every gate check performed.
Hardware Context
This architecture ran on consumer hardware — a mini PC with modest GPU. The three-tier node structure (3B/8B/14B) was designed specifically so the system could route lightweight requests to smaller faster models and reserve larger models for requests that genuinely required them. This kept the system responsive on hardware that couldn't run large models for every interaction.
The same principle informs the current AxiomOS design — right-sized model for the task, escalation only when necessary, constitutional enforcement at every step.
